---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Practice Lab | Statement Lab" description="Interactive exercises for financial-report literacy.">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Practice lab</p><h1>Turn concepts into instincts.</h1><p class="lead">Try an answer, request a hint, then reveal the explanation. Your attempt is kept only in this browser.</p></section>
  <section class="lab-grid">
    <article class="lab-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Transaction mapper</p><h2>What changes when a company buys inventory for cash?</h2><div class="choice-row" data-mapper><button data-answer="assets">Assets increase; expense increases</button><button data-answer="swap">Cash decreases; inventory increases</button><button data-answer="equity">Cash decreases; equity decreases</button></div><p class="feedback" data-mapper-feedback></p><button class="text-button" data-mapper-hint>Need a hint?</button></article>
    <article class="lab-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Linked statements</p><h2>Trace depreciation of $10.</h2><p>Choose the complete effect across the statements.</p><div class="choice-row" data-linked><button data-answer="wrong">Cash falls $10 immediately</button><button data-answer="right">Profit falls $10; asset carrying value falls $10; cash flow adds it back</button><button data-answer="wrong2">Revenue falls $10; cash rises $10</button></div><p class="feedback" data-linked-feedback></p></article>
    <article class="lab-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Ratio workbench</p><h2>Calculate the current ratio.</h2><div class="inputs"><label>Current assets <input inputmode="decimal" data-ca value="240" /></label><label>Current liabilities <input inputmode="decimal" data-cl value="120" /></label></div><button class="button small" data-calc>Calculate</button><p class="feedback" data-ratio-feedback></p><p class="muted">Formula: current assets ÷ current liabilities. A ratio prompts a liquidity question; it is not a verdict.</p></article>
    <article class="lab-card"><p class="eyebrow">04 · Filing detective</p><h2>Where should you investigate a sharp rise in receivables?</h2><div class="choice-row" data-filing><button data-answer="income">Income statement only</button><button data-answer="right">Receivables note, revenue policy, cash flow, and management discussion</button><button data-answer="audit">Auditor signature only</button></div><p class="feedback" data-filing-feedback></p></article>
    <article class="lab-card wide"><p class="eyebrow">05 · Scenario check</p><h2>Profit rose, but operating cash flow fell. What is the best first response?</h2><div class="choice-row" data-scenario><button data-answer="sell">Conclude the company is failing</button><button data-answer="right">Compare working capital, non-cash items, and prior periods before forming a conclusion</button><button data-answer="ignore">Ignore cash flow because profit rose</button></div><p class="feedback" data-scenario-feedback></p></article>
  </section>
  <script>import '../scripts/lab.ts';</script>
</BaseLayout>
